            <ArticleTitle>[Bronchopulmonary diseases in workers engaged into aluminium production in Transpolar area of Kolsky peninsula].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Findings are that chronic bronchitis (14.1-18.5% of workers) is leading among bronchopulmonary diseases in workers engaged into electrolysis and auxiliary workshops of aluminium production. Chronic obstructive lung disease (COLD) and bronchial asthma (BA) occur in 1.6-2.4% of the workers requiring employment. Among other variants of BA, potroom asthma--occupational form of the disease--should be emphasized. Risk of chronic bronchitis and COLD depends on length of exposure to the occupational hazards, and intensity of smoking habit.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
